# Accepted gitleaks findings, pinned by FINGERPRINT
# (<commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>) rather than by excluding a path or
# switching a rule off. gitleaks reads this file automatically from the
# root of the repository it scans, so CI and a developer running the same
# command locally accept exactly the same set — the previous home for
# this line was a heredoc inside .github/workflows/ci.yml, which only CI
# ever saw.
#
# Adding a line here is a security decision. Each one carries WHY the
# matched value is not a credential; a line without that is a suppression,
# which SPEC §5.3 does not allow.

# The generic-api-key rule matches the Samba Distribution Verification
# Key's PRIMARY FINGERPRINT on line 5 of keys/PINNING.md (SPEC §4.4). It
# is a 40-hex string with the entropy of a token and none of the secrecy
# — it is the PUBLIC pin every upstream tarball signature in this
# repository is verified against, and publishing it is the entire point
# of the file it sits in. (The value is deliberately not repeated here:
# a second copy would be a second finding, on a line no fingerprint
# covers yet — this allowlist would turn the gate red on itself.)
# Pinning the fingerprint keeps every other line of keys/PINNING.md, and
# any future commit touching this one, in scope: a key rotation produces
# a new gitleaks fingerprint and turns the gate red until a human
# re-reads it.
